On Wed, 24 Jan 2007, nyra wrote:
>
> Genocide is one of the things implemented only with player-use in
> mind; similarly, monsters won't use wishing gear, scrolls of charging
> or taming, spellbooks, wands of secret door detection, rings, amulets
> of magical breathing[1] etc. etc.

   FWIW, while I agree that monsters' using genocide or taming (on the 
player) would be a terrible idea, and spellbooks would be messy and
confusing, I think most of that other stuff is only unused because the
DevTeam hasn't gotten around to it yet. L has a monster ring patch;
an amulet patch wouldn't be any harder, and would probably be easier,
since they already wear "oLS.

> [1] imagine a yendorian frogman team patrolling the castle moat ...

   See, I think that would be cool. :)  Of course, the monsters would
have to be generated with amulets (doesn't currently happen), or else
they'd have to find them lying around (highly unlikely), so you wouldn't
actually get frogman teams in real games; but if a monster /did/ happen
to find an "oMB, I see no reason to forbid it from using the amulet.

   Even taming could be used by monsters to hostile-ify your pets;[2]
the player would of course have to be immune. Genocide should never
be used by anyone but the player, though, because the player needs
to have a perfect mental list of all the genocided species so that
controlled polyself (into a genocided species) isn't an instakill...
am I right about that?

-Arthur

[2] - I repeat my belief that the hostile/peaceful/tame mechanism needs
a total overhaul, right up there with pit-filling, item ownership, and
a portable random-access savefile format.


